<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Banu Khalid Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1669 CE – 1796 CE (approx.) · capital Hofuf</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Bedouin emirate that ruled eastern Arabia from Hofuf after expelling the Ottomans, until the first Saudi state absorbed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Banu Khalid were a powerful tribal confederation of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. In 1670 their chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barrak-ibn-ghurayr">Barrak ibn Ghurayr</a> expelled the Ottoman garrison of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lahsa-eyalet">Lahsa Eyalet</a> and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hofuf">Hofuf</a> the centre of an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> controlling the coast from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-kuwait">Kuwait</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-qatar">Qatar</a> and the oases of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Hasa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qatif">Qatif</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> governed through tribal alliances, taxing oasis farmers, pearl divers and caravans while keeping nominal ties with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Under their protection, clans of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-utbah">Bani Utbah</a> settled at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-kuwait">Kuwait</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zubarah">Zubarah</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-qatar">Qatar</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulayman-ibn-muhammad-al-hamid">Sulayman ibn Muhammad</a>, emir in the mid-18th century, pressured the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyayna">Uyayna</a> to expel the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-abd-al-wahhab">Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Family feuds after 1752 weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-diriyah">Emirate of Diriyah</a> defeated the Banu Khalid in a series of campaigns and conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Hasa</a> by 1796, though the tribe remained important in the region.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1669 CE – 1796 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.92%;width:2.53%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1669 CE – 1796 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hofuf</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Barrak ibn Ghurayr, Sulayman ibn Muhammad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>, <a href="/countries/kuwait">Kuwait</a>, <a href="/countries/qatar">Qatar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of al-Hasa, Banu Khalid</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1732&amp;focus=banu-khalid-emirate" aria-label="Banu Khalid Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5994 1245 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Banu Khalid Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6314 1501L6318 1459M6314 1501L6237 1523M6314 1501L6250 1360"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6318 1459h0M6237 1523h0M6250 1360h0"/><path class="map-dot-